CORE no-new-smt
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
SMT2 back-ends using the floating-point theory (--cprover-smt2, --bitwuzla,
--cvc5) flatten unions to bit-vectors, but encode doubles as floating-point
terms. Writing a non-constant double member used to fail an invariant in
flatten2bv, and reading one produced an ill-sorted term.
The new SMT back-end does not support extractbit yet.
